A chapter I don’t know if I’ll ever be fully ready to close…. 

Making the right decision is not always easy. Prioritizing your health over your passions or commitments, while seemingly simple, is often grueling, heartbreaking, and disappointing. Sometimes, making those decisions can be empowering and hopeful. 

Many of you know this, but for the past 6 years I have been dealing with chronic hip pain, recurrent labral tears, impingement, and so much more. I have already had two surgeries to correct these issues yet I have found myself facing another, more invasive operation next month. Competing while dealing with this grueling pain for so long not only takes a toll physically, but emotionally too. 

Therefore, after so much consideration, conversation, and reflection, I have come to the decision to forfeit my last year of eligibility and medically retire from fencing. 

This was not a decision I came to lightly, and I am still grieving. I have so much unfinished business but it is at a point where I have to make the right choice for my future. I also want to express my gratitude for all of the support I have received during my fencing journey and this new chapter I am navigating. 

@sfreedman418 I would never have starting this sport if not for you. There is so much I want to say but I’m just going to leave this here: who would have thought grocery store aisles would have turned into this. 

@ohiostatefencing Thank you for the most incredible four years. I owe so much of my growth and development as a person, student, and athlete to you. 

@elvisgregorygil Thank you for believing in me and pushing me. 

@renfencing Thank you for molding me into the fencer I was, and for helping me pave the path to international and college fencing. 

@mission_fencing Thank you for being the first to show me why this sport is so amazing. 

To my family, my fencing family, and friends: thank you for cheering me on, the tournament fruit snacks, and lending a shoulder to cry on whenever I needed it. 

If you made it to this point, thank you. This is not how I wanted my fencing journey to end, but now I am on a path to heal myself and others. 

And as always, Go Bucks❤️

